# Analytic number theory: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. Acceptance signatures
belong to the two substantive owners, AnalyticNumberTheoryPartI (Layers 0–3)
and AnalyticNumberTheoryPartII (Layers 4–6), against the pinned APIs.
This navigation index owns no headline theorem, so it declares none.

Part I states, among other headlines, finite-order Hadamard factorization,
Siegel–Walfisz, bounded-degree Brauer–Siegel and the second and fourth zeta
moments. Part II states Lerch continuation, the quadratic large sieve,
quadratic double-series functional equations and critical scaling measures.
The README links both owning signature files.

The owners also explain which headlines lack carriers at the pins: canonical
continued Hecke and Artin functions and quadratic period geometry in Part I;
arithmetic cubic-order coefficients, the completed Bost–Connes dynamical system
and the geometric scalar spectrum and Selberg product in Part II.
Their absence is a limitation of those particular signatures, not a reason to
replace the available headlines. No theorem is restated in this index.
